(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Continuous Measurement in a Potential", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A live, self-contained walk through the simulation of a quantum \
particle whose position is measured continuously and weakly, generalized from \
the free particle to any one-dimensional Hamiltonian ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 StyleBox[": we write the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation as a \
Bayesian update on a position grid, recover the free particle as the ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 StyleBox[" special case, watch a harmonic trap squeeze the conditional state \
below the vacuum while its unconditional average heats without bound, and \
watch a double well, where no finite set of moments closes, localize the \
particle in one well and freeze its tunneling by the quantum Zeno effect.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami. Last updated July 29, 2026.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook covers one topic as a continuous story: continuous weak \
measurement of a particle's position, written first as a stochastic Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation and its Bayesian update, then built into a \
split-operator simulation on a grid, then run for three Hamiltonians in turn, \
the free particle, the harmonic trap, and the double well, with the \
conditional state, the unconditional (Lindblad) average, the moment filter, \
the measurement backaction, and the quantum Zeno effect each read off a cell \
you can rerun.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell["\<\
I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, \
if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. So almost nothing \
here is asserted without a cell that computes it on the spot, and almost \
every claim is checked against an independent calculation, symbolic against \
numeric or one representation against another.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is a live Wolfram notebook, not a static paper. Evaluate the cells top \
to bottom; many depend on symbols defined earlier, so a fresh kernel wants a \
fresh top-to-bottom pass. Read it as a movie rather than a reference: each \
cell sets up the next question, and the prose between cells is the connective \
tissue, not decoration. My suggestion is to focus on each output and its \
meaning before worrying about every detail of the input code. And remember \
that the code is yours: change the potential, the measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 ", the initial state, the grid, rerun, and see what moves. That is the point."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Prerequisites are light: basic quantum mechanics (states, operators, the \
position and momentum representations) and enough Wolfram Language to read a \
one-line function. No stochastic calculus is needed beyond one fact, stated \
when we need it: over a step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " the Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " is a zero-mean Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". The pace steepens gently in Part IV, where a matrix Riccati equation is \
solved in closed form; the two companion essays ",
 StyleBox["Watching a Quantum Particle", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Trajectories, the Record, and the Master Equation", "TI"],
 " develop the free-particle case at more length and are optional background, \
not requirements. Throughout, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", the mass ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 " stay symbolic wherever the algebra is symbolic, and take numerical values \
(",
 Cell[BoxData["hbar"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["mass"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 ") only in simulation. Comments and corrections are welcome."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
Part I: The Stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger Equation: Measurement as \
Bayes' Rule\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the equation of motion. A particle with Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " whose position is measured continuously and weakly obeys a stochastic Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation (SSE), the diffusive quantum-state-diffusion \
form,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "2"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "]"}], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words: the first term is ordinary unitary evolution under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 "; the last is the stochastic measurement backaction, proportional to the \
Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ", which nudges the state toward a sharper position; and the middle term is \
the nonlinear drift whose only job is to keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " normalized. The strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " (the measurement rate) sets how fast position information arrives. The \
detector's own output over the same increment is the measurement record"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which is the conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " buried in white noise. Equivalently, the record is signal (the mean) plus \
shot noise (the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 "), and because that one increment appears in both the state equation and \
the record, the state can be reconstructed from the observed current. That \
reconstruction is quantum filtering, and it is what a real experiment \
computes in real time. We will return to the filter concretely in Part IV."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the crucial reframing, and the answer to \"where is the update?\": the \
SSE is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 " limit of a concrete two-step update, and it is the update, not the \
differential form, that the simulation runs. Over one step the detector \
returns a single weak-measurement outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ", a reading of the position blurred by Gaussian noise, and the state is \
revised by ",
 StyleBox["Bayes' rule",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The reading has likelihood"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "2", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a Gaussian in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " centered on the true position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 ". Because the reading is noisy, the outcome is not drawn from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " directly but from the ",
 StyleBox["prior predictive", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 ", the density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " convolved with the detector noise. And the conditional (posterior) density \
is the prior reweighted by the likelihood,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "\[ThickSpace]", "\[LongRightArrow]",
     "\[ThickSpace]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", 
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which is Bayes' rule verbatim: posterior ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Proportional]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Times]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " prior. At the level of amplitudes this reweighting is a Kraus operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ", the square root of the likelihood, applied and renormalized; multiplying \
each amplitude by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " carries the phase along. The particle then evolves unitarily for the step, \
so one full step is Bayes' rule followed by Hamiltonian evolution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
       "Ket"]}], GridBox[{
       {GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["(",
              SpanMaxSize->1], 
             OverscriptBox[
              StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
             StyleBox[")",
              SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
            TemplateBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
                StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
                StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
                StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
             "Ket"]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "."}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In short: measure by Bayes' rule, then evolve. Notice the one fact we will \
lean on for the rest of the notebook: the measurement half of this update \
knows nothing about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ". The outcome distribution, the Bayesian reweighting, and the \
renormalization are identical for a free particle, a trap, or a double well; \
only the unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " carries the potential. So generalizing the simulation to any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " will mean generalizing that one factor and leaving the measurement \
untouched, which is exactly what the next Part does."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell["\<\
Part II: One Function Carries the Potential: A Split-Operator Step on a Grid\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part I gave the update as an equation; to run it we have to make one \
decision that everything else follows from. A wavefunction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " is defined at every point of the infinite line, which is more than a \
computer can hold, so we keep it only on a finite grid: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " equally spaced points across a window of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 ", at spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ". The state becomes a list of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " complex numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ", and every operation below is arithmetic on that list. The care is all in \
choosing the window and the spacing, and in carrying, next to the positions, \
the momenta we will need. Let me explain each piece before writing the grid."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why a periodic box.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Cutting space to a window of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " leaves two loose ends, and we glue them: the point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " is identified with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "+", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ", so the segment becomes a ring of circumference ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 ". We choose this periodic boundary for one reason. Momentum states are the \
plane waves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 ", and on a ring such a wave is allowed only if it closes up smoothly after \
going once around, which forces the momentum onto the discrete ladder"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "\[Ellipsis]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, periodicity is exactly what turns momentum from a continuum \
into an evenly spaced list we can store beside the positions, and it makes \
those plane waves an exact basis. It costs nothing as long as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " stays negligible at the edges, so the packet never feels the seam where \
the ends are glued."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How to choose the length and the spacing.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " These answer two independent physical questions. The length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " must be large enough to hold the whole wavefunction, tails included, for \
the entire run: the packet spreads, drifts, and (under measurement) heats, \
and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " must contain all of it, or a tail that reaches one edge reappears at the \
other. The spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " must be small enough to resolve the fastest wiggle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 ", which is set by its largest momentum: a component of momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " oscillates with de Broglie wavelength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 ", and capturing a wave needs at least two samples across it, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 " small enough that the biggest momentum you expect stays below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 ". The two ends are mirror images: the box length fixes the momentum spacing \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " (fine momentum needs a big box), the sampling fixes the momentum reach ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " (high momentum needs fine sampling). So choosing the position grid already \
fixes the momentum grid, which is why one function returns both ",
 Cell[BoxData["x"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["p"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What the Fourier transform is, and why we want it.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " We will keep switching between two descriptions of the same state: how \
much amplitude sits at each position, the list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 ", and how much sits at each momentum, the coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " when we write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " as a sum of the plane waves above, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 ". The recipe that turns the first list into the second is the ",
 StyleBox["Fourier transform", "TI"],
 ": a reversible change of basis, the fixed sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " that correlates the state against each plane wave, with an inverse that \
rebuilds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How a wavefunction sits on the grid.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " After all that, representing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " is the easy part: evaluate it at the grid points and normalize, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "=", "1"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ". That list is the state in the position description; its Fourier transform \
is the same state in the momentum description. First fix units so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mass", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define he grid given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " the space and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["l", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 " the size of the box:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "l_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"l", "/", "n"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<dx\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dx"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "l"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The grid itself returns an association with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ", the spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", the positions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "{", "-", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2", "-", "1", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " (centered on the origin, so the box is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 "), and the quantized momenta ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", " ", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ". The momenta are stored rotated, nonnegative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 " first and the negative half moved to the end, because that is the order ",
 Cell[BoxData["Fourier"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 " returns them in, so that later one multiplication lands each amplitude on \
its own momentum."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A convenient initial state is a Gaussian wave packet centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " with mean momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " and position width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ". Following the recipe just above, we write its formula on the grid points ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 " and normalize:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], ")"}],
          "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "/", "hbar"}]}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two numbers we will watch most are the conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " and the conditional variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ". On the grid each is a dot product against the probability density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the measurement step, we implement it in the two pieces: first the \
outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 ", then the Bayesian update of the state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " is a sample from the prior predictive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 ". Recall that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 " convolved with Gaussian noise of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ". So for the sampling of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 ", we can treat it as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " distributed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " distributed as a Gaussian with zero mean and standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second the Bayesian update itself: reweight the amplitudes by the square \
root of the likelihood, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ", and renormalize. That is the whole measurement step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Lambda]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], ")"}], 
        "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Is this really Bayes' rule? It should be: the updated density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"p", "o", "s", "t"}], "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 " ought to equal the prior ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " times the likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 ", normalized. Confirm the two constructions agree, for a test state and \
outcome:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gDemo", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"512", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\[Psi]t", ",", 
     " ", "post", ",", " ", "bayes", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", ".75"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", ".01"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", ".5"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]t", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gDemo", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "2."}], 
      "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"post", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "gDemo", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
         "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]t", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"bayes", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gDemo", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], 
            ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "Total"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"post", " ", "-", " ", "bayes"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference is at machine level, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["measUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 " is exactly the Bayesian posterior; the operator form and the \"likelihood \
times prior\" form are two representations of the same update."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two small diagnostics will be handy later: the norm error (how far ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {GridBox[{
       {
        TemplateBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
         "Ket"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " strays from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 ") and the density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " built from a state vector. Define both:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"normError", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"projector", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " the potential is diagonal in position, so its propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " is just a pointwise phase. Define aa half-step of it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Vfun", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's explain why the half-step. To approximate one step of the true \
dynamics, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ", we use the Trotter-Suzuki formula: a family of operator-splitting methods \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 " when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"h", "B"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " are each easy to compute but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " do not commute. Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " are the kinetic and potential generators and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ". The first-order member of the family of operator-splitting is the \
Lie-Trotter splitting, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "1"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "B"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ", with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " per step and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " over a fixed total time. The symmetric second-order member is the Strang \
splitting, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 ", with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "3"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 " and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 ". More generally, higher-order Suzuki compositions give an order-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " method with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 ", the one lost power coming from the roughly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 " steps needed to cover a fixed interval. We want a global error of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ", so we take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 ", the Strang splitting: with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", "\[HBar]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 ", a half potential kick around a full kinetic drift, and it is exact \
whenever ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "@*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "@*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One full conditional step is now described as follows: draw an outcome, \
apply the Bayesian ",
 Cell[BoxData["measUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 ", then ",
 Cell[BoxData["evolveStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 ". Define the step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", 
      " ", "xb_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A whole experimental run is that step iterated ",
 Cell[BoxData["nt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 " times from an initial state, with a fresh outcome drawn at each step. One \
runner does it: ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " returns the sequence of conditional states and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 "s each measurement outcome as it goes, so a bare call gives just the \
states, while wrapping it in ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reap"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 " hands back the states together with the record. Define it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", 
      " ", "nt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sow", "@", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"drawExact", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
           "#", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
     "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That is the entire engine. Everything below is these functions with a \
different ",
 Cell[BoxData["Vfun"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 ", a different initial state, or a different measurement strength."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell["\<\
Part III: The Free Particle: The V=0 Case, Recovered and Heated\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's exercise the engine on the case we already understand analytically, \
the free particle, by passing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 " for the potential. The point is twofold: to see the generalized code \
reproduce the known free-particle physics, and to build the unconditional \
(master-equation) machinery we will reuse in the trap and the well."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first known fact: under measurement a broad packet localizes to a \
steady conditional width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 ". Run one trajectory from a wide (width ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ") packet and track its conditional width over the run:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "50."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nt", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"statesF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", 
        " ", "nt"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"widthsF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     "statesF"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the width and show it approaches the predicted steady value, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"widthsF", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{".5", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nt", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<conditional width\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A broad packet localizes to the steady width (dashed)\>\""}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
            "^", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"nt", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
            "^", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And the substantive guarantee of the split-operator step, which a \
general-purpose integrator does not give, is that the norm still sits at ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"normError", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Last", "@", "statesF"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["\<\
The measured end width lands on the prediction, and the norm holds to machine \
precision. At unit detection efficiency the conditional state stays pure, \
which is what lets us carry it as a single state vector; the state only \
becomes mixed when we average over the noise, which is the master equation, \
coming next.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To average, we need the unconditional state as a density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 ". Discarding the record and averaging the conditional states over the \
Wiener noise gives the Lindblad master equation, which integrates by the same \
operator split: the measurement dissipator damps each element ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " by the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "-", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ", and the Hamiltonian acts as ",
 Cell[BoxData["evolveStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " turned into a matrix. Define the damping factor first:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"decohereMat", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Turn ",
 Cell[BoxData["evolveStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " into a matrix by applying it to each basis vector, and assemble one \
master-equation step as \"damp, then evolve on both sides\":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"uniMat", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lindblad", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}],
    " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"uniMat", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dec", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"decohereMat", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"u", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", "dec"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "u", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Position observables read straight off ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 "'s diagonal, but momentum observables like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " need the momentum-squared operator as a matrix, built spectrally:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the second known fact, the measurement backaction. Propagate the free \
master equation from a pure packet and watch its momentum variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " climb to the predicted final value:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"32", ",", " ", "16."}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dtS", " ", "=", " ", "0.0005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ntS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dtS"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]free", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lindblad", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtS"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"projector", "[", "\[Psi]0", "]"}], ",", " ", "ntS"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"pred", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]0", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "gS", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "\[Psi]0"}], "]"}], 
      " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], " ", "tf"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "gS", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
      " ", "\[Rho]free"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "tf"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8p\.b2\:27e9\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Measurement heats momentum linearly (predicted value \
dashed)\>\""}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "pred"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tf", ",", " ", "pred"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The momentum variance rises exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "0"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 ": position measurement feeds momentum at the constant rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 ", the price the uncertainty principle charges for position information. \
That rate is state- and Hamiltonian-independent, so for the free particle, \
whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 " commutes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 ", it is the whole story. In a potential it is not: the force couples ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 " as the packet swings, which is why Part V follows the total energy \
instead. This backaction is the one piece of physics common to every case \
below; we meet it again competing with the trap and with tunneling."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One more thing the engine handles that a moment method cannot: an \
arbitrary, non-Gaussian initial state. Take a \"cat,\" a superposition of two \
packets sitting at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 ". Build it and look at its two lobes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "50."}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Cat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "6."}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}], " ", "+",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", "6.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}],
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Cat", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gC", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gC", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Psi](x)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A cat state: two packets at x = \[PlusMinus]6\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its initial variance is large, dominated by that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 " lobe separation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", "\[Psi]Cat"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now watch the measurement collapse it. Take a moderate strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0.1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 ", chosen so the two lobes coexist for a visible stretch before one wins \
rather than collapsing in the first few steps, and run one trajectory:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"statesC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "0.1", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ",
         "600"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Cat", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "See the collapse as a surface of the conditional density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 " over position and time:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"band", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{"10", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gC", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListPlot3D", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "statesC", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ")"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "6"}], ",", " ", "band"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gC", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"First", "@", "band"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Last", "@", "band"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "\"\<DarkRainbow\>\"", "]"}], "[", "#3", 
       "]"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<|\[Psi]|\.b2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<A cat collapses to one packet\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell["\<\
The two ridges compete and one grows while the other fades, with no potential \
in sight.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That surface is the particle's actual density, which no experiment can see. \
What an observer sees is the record, the stream of noisy outcomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 ", and from it alone they must infer which lobe won. That inference is a \
running bet between two hypotheses, the left lobe at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "=", "-", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 " against the right at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "=", "+", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 ". Each outcome has likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["h", "TI"]]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 " under hypothesis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["h", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],
 ", so the log-odds for left over right accumulate one term at a time: each \
term is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 " times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "+", "6"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "6"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],
 ", which is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"24", " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 ", so the increment is simply ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "48", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 ". Rerun the same trajectory, keep its outcomes, and accumulate them into \
the posterior ",
 Cell[BoxData["PleftRec"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 "; first look at the raw stream the detector logs:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"catStates", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "catOuts", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "0.1", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", 
         " ", "600"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Cat", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PleftRec", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"LogisticSigmoid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "48"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", "0.1", ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", "0.005", ")"}], " ", "catOuts"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"catOuts", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<measurement step k\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<outcome\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The raw record: signal buried in noise\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That raw stream is almost pure noise: each reading scatters with standard \
deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 ", far wider than the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 " lobe separation, so no single outcome names the lobe. The verdict lives \
only in the slow average that ",
 Cell[BoxData["PleftRec"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " accumulates, which the grid's own final ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 " should confirm, ending negative for the left lobe:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Last", "@", "catStates"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the record says ",
 StyleBox["left lobe", "TI"],
 " and the grid agrees. The road there is the instructive part: the belief \
builds only over many steps, and can even lean the wrong way first. Plot the \
posterior forming over the first many steps, from the even prior ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
     RowBox[{"PleftRec", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "120"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "119"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "Gray"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<measurement step k\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<observer's posterior P_left\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The record decides the lobe (here \[RightArrow] 1, the left \
lobe won)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell["\<\
The posterior leaves the even prior, wavers toward the right lobe as the \
first noisy readings arrive, then swings over and pins to the left lobe as \
the evidence piles up. The observer never touched the wavefunction, only the \
noisy current, yet reconstructed which packet survived.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That verdict was this record's; a different noise history would decide \
differently. The initial cat is symmetric, so nothing favors either lobe: the \
measurement forces a definite choice, but which lobe is set entirely by the \
noise. Overlay several independent seeded records and watch their posteriors \
split, some pinning to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " (left), some to ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " (right):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "k", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"LogisticSigmoid", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "48"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", "0.1", ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", "0.005", ")"}], "\n", "        ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "0.1", ",", " ", "0.005", ",",
                " ", "100"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Cat", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "Gray"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<measurement step k\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<P_left\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Different records, different verdicts\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell["\<\
The runs split between the two lobes, each driven to a definite outcome by \
its own record. This is the measurement record doing the observer's \
inference, the same accumulation a real detector performs in software. Now we \
turn on a potential and ask what survives.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell["\<\
Part IV: The Harmonic Trap: Measurement That Squeezes Below the Vacuum\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A trapped particle is never still: even in its ground state its position \
keeps the irreducible zero-point spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "p"}], "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 ", the blur of the quantum vacuum. So here is the question this Part \
answers: ",
 StyleBox["watch that position continuously, and can you come to know it more \
sharply than the vacuum itself allows? What does the state become?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The harmonic trap is where this can be settled exactly. Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 " is quadratic, a Gaussian conditional state stays Gaussian under both the \
measurement update and the evolution, so the entire state collapses to five \
numbers, the two means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " and the three covariances ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], ",", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],
 ", and we can solve their steady state with algebra before ever touching the \
grid. (This is also the real setting of cavity and levitated optomechanics, \
where light monitors a mechanical mode.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the covariances, and the fact that makes the trap solvable: they \
close among themselves. The rates for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "}"}]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 " depend only on each other, never on the means or the noise, so they run \
deterministically (a matrix Riccati flow). Write the three rates, keeping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], ",", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],
 " symbolic, and solve for the fixed point where all three vanish:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p", ",", " ",
     "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "\[Omega]", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "\[HBar]"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"riccati", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cc", "/", "m"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]p", "/", "m"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x"}], " ", "-", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x", " ", "Cc"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "m", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", "Cc"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cc", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"steady", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"riccati", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Solve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " returns several algebraic roots; the physical one has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 ". Select it by a quick numeric probe and simplify the result symbolically:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"posRoot", "[", "rule_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], 
          "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", "rule"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "1."}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Im", "[", "v", "]"}]}]}], " ", "<", " ", 
       RowBox[{"10", "^", 
        RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
        RowBox[{"v", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
        RowBox[{"v", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[CapitalSigma]xSS", ",", " ", "CcSS", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]pSS"}], 
   "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], 
      "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"First", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
       RowBox[{"steady", ",", " ", "posRoot"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first entry is the steady position variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"s", "s"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     SqrtBox["2"]}]], 
   SqrtBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
      SqrtBox[
       RowBox[{"4", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "4"]}]]}], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],
 ". Two checks that it is right. First, perfect measurement keeps the state \
pure, and a pure Gaussian sits exactly at the uncertainty floor, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],
 " must come out to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]pSS"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"CcSS", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And switching off the trap, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 ", should return the free-particle steady value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both check out: the steady state is a pure Gaussian that reduces to the \
free particle when the trap is switched off. Now the payoff, the question we \
opened with. Set the steady variance against the vacuum value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "p"}], "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],
 ": form the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"s", "s"}], "TI"]], "/", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "p"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 " and simplify:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Mu]", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[HBar]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "m", " ", "\[Omega]"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the single dimensionless measurement strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],
 " that is exactly the clean closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 "; confirm the two are equal:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "m", " ", "\[Omega]"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
        ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", "\[Mu]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That ratio is below ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],
 " for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],
 ". Its two limiting regimes follow by expanding the closed form (writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 " as a bare expansion variable):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "q", "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
               RowBox[{"q", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
            ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", "q"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"q", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That is the weak limit, dipping just below the zero-point value as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 " grows from zero. For strong measurement, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],
 ", the ratio itself vanishes; the telling quantity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 " times it, which should approach a constant:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "q", "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "q", "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"q", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], 
        "]"}], "/", "q"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"q", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the ratio is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[TildeTilde]", "1", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "2"], "/", "8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],
 " for weak watching and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[TildeTilde]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"2", "/", 
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " for strong. There is the answer to our question, stated plainly: \
continuous position measurement pushes the conditional variance below the \
vacuum at ",
 StyleBox["any", "TI"],
 " strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 ", and deeper the harder you watch. The conditional state is a pure squeezed \
state, narrower in position than the ground state itself, because the \
measurement is steadily extracting position information. Fix a \
strongly-measured regime, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 " (so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],
 "), and read the position variance in units of the vacuum:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xZP", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "\[Omega]R"}], ")"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]pZP", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "mass", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"harmNum", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", " ", "->", " ", "hbar"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "->", " ", "mass"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "->", " ", "\[Omega]R"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "\[Lambda]R"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", " ", "/.", " ", "harmNum"}], ")"}], "/", 
  "\[CapitalSigma]xZP"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Below ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 ": squeezed below the vacuum. The price shows in the momentum, anti-squeezed \
above its own zero-point value by the reciprocal cost:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]pSS", " ", "/.", " ", "harmNum"}], ")"}], "/", 
  "\[CapitalSigma]pZP"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],

Cell["\<\
The position is squeezed well below the zero-point variance and the momentum \
is anti-squeezed above it: the backaction paid for the position information. \
All of this came from the closed-form moments. Does the grid engine, which \
assumes nothing about Gaussianity, agree? Evolve one trajectory from the \
ground state in the trap and read the late-time conditional variance:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Vharm", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0.5", " ", "mass", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"#", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gH", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "24."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtH", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfH", " ", "=", " ", "8."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ntH", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tfH", "/", "dtH"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"runH", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "gH", ",", " ", "Vharm", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtH", ",", 
        " ", "ntH"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xH", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "runH"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xH", "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.6", " ", "ntH"}], "]"}], " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That late-time grid variance should match the closed-form Riccati steady \
value and sit below the zero-point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "p"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 "; read the two reference values side by side:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", " ", "/.", " ", "harmNum"}], ",", " ", 
   "\[CapitalSigma]xZP"}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell["\<\
The grid variance relaxes to the Riccati steady value, matching it to grid \
resolution and sitting well below the zero-point. The relaxation is the same \
in every run, because the conditional variance obeys a deterministic \
(noiseless) equation while only the mean is driven by the record. Plot the \
variance against time with the zero-point and Riccati lines drawn in:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dtH", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "ntH"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "\[CapitalSigma]xH"}], "}"}], "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0.55"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xZP", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]xSS", " ", "/.", " ", "harmNum"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<conditional variance \[CapitalSigma]x\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Measurement squeezes \[CapitalSigma]x below the zero-point line \
(gray) to the Riccati value (red)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The grid agreed, but it was never needed: the whole conditional state is \
those five numbers, the two means driven by the record and the three \
covariances running on their own. This five-number object is the quantum \
Kalman-Bucy filter, the algorithm an optomechanics experiment integrates in \
real time to track its mechanical mode from the measurement current. Hand its \
equations to the stochastic integrator ",
 Cell[BoxData["ItoProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],
 ", the drifts in place and the noise entering only through the means:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "mx", ",", " ", "mp", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", 
    " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"momentProc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"mp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "mass"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", 
         "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]p", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}], " ", "-",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"mass", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "mass", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
        "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mp", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cc", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]p", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "mx", ",", " ", "mp", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",",
          " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", ",", " ", "0.", 
         ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]pZP"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],

Cell["\<\
Integrate an ensemble of these filters and read the mean conditional variance \
across the ensemble together with its run-to-run spread:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tdM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
      RowBox[{"momentProc", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tfH", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "300", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
       "Method", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"finM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"tdM", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "finM"}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "finM"}], 
    "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean sits on the Riccati value and the spread is exactly zero: every \
realization carries the ",
 StyleBox["same", "TI"],
 " variance. Contrast the conditional mean, which spreads freely across runs \
because it is the part the record drives:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "finM"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Grid, filter, and algebra return the same variance, and across the ensemble \
that variance has exactly zero spread while the mean wanders freely from run \
to run. That is the division of labor made visible: the covariance is fixed \
and deterministic, and all the randomness lives in the means, fed by the \
record through the gains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 ". Five numbers and a 256-point grid describe the same state, because for a \
quadratic trap the Gaussian picture is exact. One honest caveat from the lab: \
we assumed perfect detection, which is what keeps the state pure and below \
the vacuum. A real experiment collects only a fraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 " of the light, mixing the conditional state and lifting its uncertainty \
back above the vacuum (Magrini et al. measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["1.3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],
 " times zero-point), the extension we return to at the close."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell["Closing the Loop: The Record Reconstructs the State", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The filter above ran on its own manufactured noise, so it showed that the \
covariances agree but never that the ",
 StyleBox["same", "TI"],
 " record rebuilds the ",
 StyleBox["same", "TI"],
 " conditional mean. That reconstruction, the observer recovering the state \
from the current, is the whole point of quantum filtering and the promise \
Part I made here. Deliver it in two steps: first confirm the record carries \
exactly the noise the theory claims, then feed that record to the filter and \
watch it track the grid."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one long trajectory in the trap, this time keeping every measurement \
outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 " next to the conditional mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 " the grid computes on the spot:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"recStates", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "recOuts", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "21", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "gH", ",", " ", "Vharm", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtH", ",",
          " ", "ntH"}], "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xGrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "recStates"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The record is those outcomes assembled into a current. Over one step the \
integrated signal is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 ", and its ",
 StyleBox["innovation", "TI"],
 ", the part no filter could have predicted, is what is left after \
subtracting the expected signal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The theory is specific about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 ": it should be the bare Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],
 ", mean zero, variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 ", uncorrelated from one step to the next. The variance follows from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 " of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 ", giving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], "\[CenterDot]", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],
 ". First its mean and variance: the mean should read near ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],
 " and the variance-over-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 " ratio near ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]Y", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", "dtH", " ", "recOuts"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]Y", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Most", "[", "xGrid", "]"}], " ", "dtH"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "\[CapitalDelta]W", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Variance", "[", "\[CapitalDelta]W", "]"}], "/", "dtH"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell["\<\
And successive steps should be uncorrelated; the lag-1 through lag-4 \
autocorrelations should all sit near zero:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Correlation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "k"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The innovation comes out with mean consistent with zero, variance \
consistent with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " to within the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"2", "/", 
     StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],
 " sampling scatter of a finite run, and lag autocorrelations that all sit \
inside the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],
 " band of true white noise. The record is signal plus white noise, exactly \
as posed. (At finite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],
 " the intrinsic conditional spread lifts the variance by a further ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],
 ", a fraction that is below the sampling floor here and vanishes as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],
 ".) Two pictures make the point: scaled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 " the innovation histogram is a standard normal, and its autocorrelation is \
flat."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dtH", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "60", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<PDF\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PDF", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"z", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", "Red"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalDelta]W / \[Sqrt]dt\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Innovations are standard-normal (red curve)\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Correlation", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]W", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "20"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Filling", " ", "->", " ", "Axis"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "0.05"}], ",", " ", "0.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "\[CapitalDelta]W", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<autocorrelation\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<No structure across lags (\[PlusMinus]2/\[Sqrt]N band)\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[48]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the reconstruction. Hand the filter the recorded increments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],
 " and nothing else, integrating the mean equations"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["f", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["f", "TI"]]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "in which the filter forms its own innovation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["f", "TI"]], "=", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 " from its current estimate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 ", and the covariances ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], ",", 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 " follow the same deterministic Riccati flow as before, independent of the \
record. Write the covariance drift and one filter step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"covDrift", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalSigma]x_", ",", " ", "Cc_", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cc", "/", "mass"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]x", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalSigma]p", "/", "mass"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mass", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x"}], " ", "-", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x", " ", "Cc"}]}], 
     ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "mass", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", "Cc"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", 
       RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cc", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"filterStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "mx_", ",", " ", "mp_", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x_", ",", " ", "Cc_", 
       ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p_"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     "\[CapitalDelta]Yk_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dWf", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]Yk", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", "mx", " ", 
          "dtH"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cov", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}], 
          "}"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dtH", " ", 
          RowBox[{"covDrift", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[CapitalSigma]x", ",", " ", "Cc", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]p"}],
            "]"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mx", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"mp", "/", "mass"}], " ", "dtH"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", "\[CapitalSigma]x", " ",
          "dWf"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mp", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mass", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", "mx", " ", "dtH"}], " ", "+", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Lambda]R", "]"}], " ", "Cc", " ", "dWf"}]}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cov", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[49]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell["\<\
Fold that step along the recorded increments from the ground state, and \
compare the filter's mean to the grid's:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mFilter", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
     RowBox[{"filterStep", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", ",", " ", "0.", ",",
         " ", "\[CapitalSigma]pZP"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\[CapitalDelta]Y"}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mFilter", " ", "-", " ", "xGrid"}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[50]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That maximum deviation only means something against the range over which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],
 " itself swings, so read the swing too:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Min", "@", "xGrid"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "@", "xGrid"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[51]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Driven by the recorded current alone, the five-number filter reproduces the \
grid's conditional mean to a small fraction of the range over which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 " itself swings: the residual is set by the grid spacing and the step size, \
not by anything statistical. The same record the grid produced, fed to a \
filter that never sees the wavefunction, rebuilds the same trajectory of the \
mean. That is quantum filtering in one line of physics: the experiment \
measures the current, the filter integrates five numbers in real time, and \
out comes the conditional state. Overlay the two and they lie on top of each \
other:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dtH", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "ntH"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "xGrid"}], "}"}],
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dtH", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "ntH"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "mFilter"}], 
       "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GrayLevel", "[", "0.6", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<grid \:27e8x\:27e9\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<filter m_x from the record\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<conditional mean position\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<One record, two engines: the filter reconstructs the grid's \
\:27e8x\:27e9(t)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[52]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],

Cell["\<\
Part V: Backaction in the Trap: An Unconditional State That Never Settles\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional state settled into a steady squeezed pure state. It is \
natural to expect the unconditional state, the average over the record, to \
settle too, perhaps into a thermal state. It does not, and seeing why is \
worth a moment. The trap conserves energy on its own, but the measurement \
backaction keeps injecting energy the closed trap has no way to remove. Watch \
this in the moments: the unconditional second moments close by themselves, \
and their energy has a constant source. Solve the unconditional moment \
equations in closed form and read the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"XX", ",", " ", "SS", ",", " ", "PP"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"usol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"XX", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SS", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SS", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"PP", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"XX", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"PP", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "m", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"SS", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"XX", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "x0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SS", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"PP", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "p0"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"XX", ",", " ", "SS", ",", " ", "PP"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}],
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"energy", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PP", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "m", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"XX", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", "/.", " ", "usol"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[53]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is linear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],
 ", so its time derivative should be a constant, the steady heating rate:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"D", "[", 
   RowBox[{"energy", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[54]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The energy is exactly linear in time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],
 ", with no oscillatory part: the breathing of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 " against each other cancels in the sum, leaving only steady heating at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 ". Equivalently, the mean occupation climbs linearly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],
 ": the unconditional state is a mixed Gaussian whose energy and mean \
occupation grow without bound. With no damping and no detailed balance there \
is no thermodynamic temperature to assign, so it is thermal-like only in its \
Gaussian shape, not a thermal state. Confirm it on the grid by propagating \
the master equation and reading the energy and the individual moments at a \
few times. First two observables on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],
 ", position-squared as a diagonal expectation and the energy:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gHL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"96", ",", " ", "24."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtHL", " ", "=", " ", "0.002"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x2Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Rho]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Emeas", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "gHL", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0.5", " ", "mass", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]R", "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"x2Mean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gHL", ",", " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[55]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell["Now propagate from the ground state and tabulate:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0HL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"projector", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
     RowBox[{"gHL", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tsHL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "0.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "1.5", ",", " ", "2."}], 
    "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]sHL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lindblad", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "gHL", ",", " ", "Vharm", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dtHL"}],
          "]"}], ",", " ", "#1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#2", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"#2", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "dtHL"}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "   ", "\[Rho]0HL", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tsHL", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Emeas", " ", "/@", " ", "\[Rho]sHL"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gHL", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      "\[Rho]sHL"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ".", 
          RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "gHL", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", "\[Rho]sHL"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ".", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      "\[Rho]sHL"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<E\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\:27e8x\.b2\:27e9\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\:27e8p\.b2\:27e9\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity\>\""}], "}"}],
       ",", " ", "tsHL"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As predicted, the energy climbs in equal steps over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],
 ", a straight ramp of slope exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],
 "; both ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],
 " grow, and the purity falls from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],
 " as the unconditional state mixes. There is no steady state to plot, only a \
ramp:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"tsHL", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Emeas", " ", "/@", " ", "\[Rho]sHL"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<unconditional energy E(t)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The trapped unconditional state heats linearly: dE/dt = \
\[Lambda]\[HBar]\.b2/2m\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note the contrast with Part IV, which is starker here than for the free \
particle: one realization sits forever in a fixed pure squeezed packet, while \
the average over realizations heats without bound. A genuine thermal ",
 StyleBox["steady", "TI"],
 " state needs a mechanical damping channel to balance the heating, which is \
exactly why the optomechanics experiments cool with feedback rather than \
watch the bare measurement; restoring that damping is a one-line addition to \
the master equation and the natural next extension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],

Cell["\<\
Before we move on, let us summarize what the two quadratic cases, free and \
harmonic, have taught us:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement half of the update is Bayes' rule, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "\[Rule]", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],
 ", and it is independent of the Hamiltonian; only the unitary carries the \
potential, recovered exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Continuous position measurement heats the momentum at the state-independent \
rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "0"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the harmonic trap the conditional state is a pure squeezed Gaussian with \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"s", "s"}], "TI"]], "/", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"z", "p"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],
 ", below the zero-point for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],
 " is quadratic the Gaussian moments close, so the five-number Kalman-Bucy \
filter is exact and agrees with the 256-point grid."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The unconditional trapped state has no steady state; it heats linearly at \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],

Cell["\<\
Every one of these rested on the moments closing. The next Part removes that.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],

Cell["\<\
Part VI: The Double Well: Where the Moments Fail and the Grid Wins\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Introduce a quartic potential and the Gaussian description breaks. For a \
double well ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],
 " the force is cubic, so the equation for the mean momentum needs the third \
moment, which a non-Gaussian state does not fix from its mean and variance. \
See it directly by differentiating the potential. The double-well force is \
cubic:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "a", ",", " ", "b"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"D", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"b", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"a", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "x"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", "4", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "3"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],
 " pulls in the third moment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "3"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],
 ". The harmonic force, by contrast, is linear and closes the hierarchy at \
the first moment:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"D", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "m", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "x"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[59]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Where the harmonic force ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],
 " closes the hierarchy at the first moment, the cubic force ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],
 " pulls in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "3"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],
 ", which pulls in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "4"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],
 ", and no finite set of moments closes. There is no five-number filter here; \
only the grid split-operator scheme, which never assumes a shape for the \
conditional state, applies. Set up the well, with minima at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],
 " and a barrier between them, and the mask that measures how much \
probability sits in the left well. Weight the single barrier-top point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],
 " by one half (it belongs to neither well), so a left-right symmetric state \
registers exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"l", "e", "f", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],
 " instead of missing that point; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sign", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],
 " does this in one Listable stroke, returning ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "<", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"aa", " ", "=", " ", "1.2"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"bb", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Vdw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"bb", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"aa", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"leftMask", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sign", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],

Cell["\<\
We will want the well's two lowest eigenstates on two different grids, so \
package the diagonalization once as a helper that returns the Hamiltonian, \
the two lowest energies, the symmetric and antisymmetric states, and their \
one-well combination:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wellDoublet", "[", "g_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "ham", ",", " ", "ev", ",", " ", "vec", ",", " ", "ord", ",", " ", 
       "sym", ",", " ", "anti"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ham", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "g", "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Vdw", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"ev", ",", " ", "vec"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Eigensystem", "[", "ham", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ord", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Ordering", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Re", "@", "ev"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"sym", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
        RowBox[{"vec", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"ord", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"anti", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
        RowBox[{"vec", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"ord", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "ham"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<E\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"ev", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"ord", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
           "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<sym\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "sym"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<anti\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "anti"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        
        RowBox[{"\"\<left\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"plus", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
               RowBox[{"sym", " ", "+", " ", "anti"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"minus", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
               RowBox[{"sym", " ", "-", " ", "anti"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
           "\n", "        ", 
           RowBox[{"If", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"leftMask", "[", "g", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "plus", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", ">=", 
              " ", "0.5"}], ",", " ", "plus", ",", " ", "minus"}], "]"}]}], 
          "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Apply it on a fine grid and read the doublet, the barrier height, the \
tunneling period ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"t", "u", "n"}], "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],
 ", and a check that the Hamiltonian is Hermitian:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gD", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "14."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"wellDoublet", "[", "gD", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Sym", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<sym\>\"", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Anti", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<anti\>\"", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Ttun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
    RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<E\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<E\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"leftP", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"leftMask", "[", "gD", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<E\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[62]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two lowest energies form a close doublet. They sit far below the \
barrier height ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],
 ", and their splitting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],
 " fixes the tunneling period ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"t", "u", "n"}], "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],
 "; read the barrier and the period:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"bb", " ", 
    RowBox[{"aa", "^", "4"}]}], ",", " ", "Ttun"}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[63]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A validity check: the Hamiltonian should be Hermitian to machine precision, \
so its spectrum is real and the ",
 Cell[BoxData["Re"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],
 " above only strips rounding:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<H\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
     RowBox[{"dw", "[", "\"\<H\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[64]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two lowest states form a doublet split by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],
 ", far below the barrier height, so a particle prepared in one well tunnels \
to the other with period ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"t", "u", "n"}], "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   "\[CapitalDelta]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],
 ". The Hamiltonian is Hermitian to machine precision, so its spectrum is \
real and the ",
 Cell[BoxData["Re"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],
 " above only strips rounding. Now confirm the claim that forecloses the \
moment filter: under measurement the conditional state is genuinely \
non-Gaussian. Track the skewness and excess kurtosis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],
 " along a measured trajectory (both are zero for a Gaussian):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"central", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]_", ",", " ", "k_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mu", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gD", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gD", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "mu"}], ")"}], 
       "^", "k"}], " ", ".", " ", "d"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"skew", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"central", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gD", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"exkurt", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"central", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gD", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ",
     "3"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"trajDW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "gD", ",", " ", "Vdw", ",", " ", "2.", ",", " ", "0.002", ",", " ", 
        "1500"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gD", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "aa"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.45"}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"skew", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"trajDW", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "100"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[65]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],

Cell["\<\
That largest skewness magnitude runs to order one, far from the Gaussian \
value of zero. The excess kurtosis does the same:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"exkurt", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"trajDW", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "100"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[66]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],

Cell["\<\
Both run to order one, far from the Gaussian value of zero: a five-number \
filter that forces skewness and kurtosis to zero cannot represent this state, \
and only the grid survives. With that established, watch the two physical \
effects of watching a particle in a double well. First, measurement-induced \
localization. Prepare the symmetric eigenstate, spread equally over both \
wells, and monitor it repeatedly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The symmetric eigenstate starts balanced over the two wells; the \
half-weighted centre point makes that exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"l", "e", "f", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"leftP", "[", "\[Psi]Sym", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[67]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now monitor it across eight measured runs at a moderate strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],
 ", chosen so the two wells coexist for a visible stretch before one wins, \
over a run kept short enough (to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "1.6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],
 ") that the backaction has not yet heated the particle over the barrier. \
Each run should localize toward one well, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"l", "e", "f", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],
 " near ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ac66077-3bfa-1f18-2afe-7a31bd8f6262"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d863d84-94ab-5643-6bbd-b4ee1d5e3ca9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"locRuns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "10", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "gD", ",", " ", "Vdw", ",", " ", "2.", ",", " ", "0.002", ",", " ", 
           "800"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Sym", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "8", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"leftP", " ", "/@", " ", "locRuns"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[68]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7ab8b877-e011-189c-2a47-323091a46ae6"],

Cell["\<\
The runs localize, each toward one well or the other, and every conditional \
state stays a normalized pure state (only the ensemble average, as in Part V, \
is mixed). Different records send the particle to different wells: the \
measurement resolves a delocalized state into a definite, if random, \
location. Two runs side by side show the density localizing, each to \
whichever well its record selects:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35eb0178-2238-e094-63e8-992257b2b2fe"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bandD", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{"3.5", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gD", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"showRun", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListPlot3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "#", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "gD", ",", " ", "Vdw", ",", " ", "2.", ",", " ", "0.002", ",", 
             " ", "800"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Sym", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "bandD"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gD", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"First", "@", "bandD"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Last", "@", "bandD"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "\"\<DarkRainbow\>\"", "]"}], "[", "#3", 
         "]"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<|\[Psi]|\.b2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<run \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "seed", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"GraphicsRow", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"showRun", "[", "4", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"showRun", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[69]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0da6433d-a7a4-ba24-3b5e-5b66d256090e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second, the quantum Zeno effect: watching the particle suppresses the \
coherent tunneling between wells. The cleanest way to see it is the \
unconditional (Lindblad) population, which is deterministic and needs no \
averaging. Recall from Part III that the dissipator dephases position; here \
it dephases the left-right coherence at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "462f64f6-435d-c7dd-6fd5-7db076e9ad27"],
 ", converting coherent oscillation into slow incoherent equilibration. On a \
coarser grid the dense master equation can afford, take the one-well state \
from the doublet helper and propagate it at a few measurement strengths. Set \
up the grid, the state, and the two observables:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b06bf63-5f43-ed7c-793d-374d5af7b446"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gDL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", "12."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dtDL", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Psi]Lwell", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"wellDoublet", "[", "gDL", "]"}], "[", "\"\<left\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"leftPL", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"leftMask", "[", "gDL", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"EmeasL", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"p2Op", "[", "gDL", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Vdw", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gDL", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[70]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0fd1c247-21a4-d962-35ee-e4215056a848"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Propagate over one tunneling period at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09347675-9fce-c17b-38cc-683f1a789041"],
 " (no measurement), a moderate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c597ed5-00d9-d535-5467-779fb16dbc1f"],
 ", and a strong ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c4d8d6-27c8-a0db-0efb-d1905262f221"],
 ", and tabulate the left-well population against time:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d3801b6-8b23-0df3-74c7-98f02ed657d9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"smp", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Ttun", "/", "dtDL"}], "/", "8"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"zenoStates", "[", "\[Lambda]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lindblad", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "gDL", ",", " ", "Vdw", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dtDL"}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", "smp"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"projector", "[", "\[Psi]Lwell", "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zTimes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], " ", "smp", " ", "dtDL"}]}], ";", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"zStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"zenoStates", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "4."}], "}"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
       RowBox[{"leftPL", ",", " ", "zStates", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "zTimes"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
   ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<P_left, \[Lambda]=0\>\"", ",",
         " ", "\"\<\[Lambda]=0.5\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Lambda]=4\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[71]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"09816d05-11e9-fb6e-3fbe-856fa79dc9b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read the columns. Without measurement the left-well population oscillates \
coherently, swinging from almost fully in the left well to almost fully in \
the right at the half period, where the particle has tunneled across, and \
back. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35ec423d-cde2-7917-6394-6466eb97487d"],
 " that coherent oscillation is gone: the population relaxes monotonically \
toward equipartition at ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.5"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05e0e9bc-56b1-1bf2-339f-00e6634469d8"],
 " and never swings across and returns. The coherent tunneling transfer is \
suppressed, which is the quantum Zeno signature of a continuous position \
measurement: watching destroys the phase coherence the tunneling needs. But \
there is a second effect competing with the first, and it is the same \
backaction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46408f14-a324-388b-6e7f-2751d6d68ad1"],
 " heating from Part V. Read the energy injected over one period, for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}], ",", "0.5", ",", "4"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40213c85-9219-7c2b-71de-b5ef27ac4771"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"678faed4-2cca-f411-0db4-479e457cdf7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"EmeasL", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "@", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
  "zStates"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[72]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3b3cac94-919f-f08d-6ac3-45de202bc2d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare those against the barrier height ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634a1270-2707-566e-1149-943a52b23cb4"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"571f0194-b08e-3ab4-7d24-98d1c138889e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bb", " ", 
  RowBox[{"aa", "^", "4"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[73]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"79764466-e076-5945-2f0e-5e4391032baf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "By one period the energy has already climbed past the barrier at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e8dec7-14b1-519a-7c97-d7a19d4423e0"],
 ", and far higher still at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f5c72f-3423-741a-538a-de89bdd65f60"],
 ": the stronger the measurement, the faster the population equilibrates over \
the top rather than through the barrier. So watching does two things at once, \
both growing with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dbbd446-5835-e39a-1b58-ce2059c1b1e0"],
 ": it dephases the wells, killing the coherent oscillation, and it heats the \
particle, eventually over the barrier. Plot the three populations to see both \
at work:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d34e655-b983-17e8-14cb-f81f38367d32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"zTimes", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"leftPL", " ", "/@", " ", "#"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
    " ", "/@", " ", "zStates"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Lambda]=0 (unwatched)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Lambda]=0.5 (dephased)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Lambda]=4 (heated over barrier)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<left-well population\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Watching kills the coherent oscillation (\[Lambda]=0.5) and, \
harder still, heats over the barrier (\[Lambda]=4)\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[74]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c435daa-0d1c-c5df-0471-54f4a4aeaf25"],

Cell["\<\
Holding the particle in one well would take the dephasing without the \
heating, and unit-efficiency position measurement cannot separate them: the \
one coupling delivers both. This is the honest reach of the Zeno effect under \
continuous position measurement, and the reason a real experiment steers with \
feedback rather than relying on the measurement alone.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21714cd0-c04e-e57a-570f-659df1f8cc40"],

Cell["\<\
Part VII: The Division of Labor: When to Filter, When to Grid\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"74ff421b-073b-c6d4-1c85-6445b2cfac3e"],

Cell["\<\
Let's recall what we have built and what it tells us to reach for. Two ways \
to simulate a continuously monitored particle appeared, and the choice \
between them is set by the Hamiltonian. When the conditional state lives in a \
small closed parametrization, the built-in stochastic integrator suffices and \
the geometry keeps the state physical on its own: a qubit is three Bloch \
numbers in a ball, and a linear (Gaussian) system, the free particle or the \
harmonic trap, is five moments whose covariance flow has an attracting \
pure-state fixed point. Both close because the Hamiltonian is at most \
quadratic, and for both the Kalman-Bucy moment filter is exact, the very \
algorithm the optomechanics experiments run.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ebc3a74-dd7c-3fa6-6643-bc31d40e858c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Otherwise, hand-write the step whose structure you can exploit. Any \
potential beyond quadratic breaks the moment closure, the conditional state \
is no longer Gaussian, and only the grid split-operator scheme applies: the \
measurement as an exact Bayesian (Kraus) update with its renormalization, \
independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d5c93fe-a057-3a16-2b63-0abbd1e3897c"],
 ", and the Hamiltonian as a Strang split whose kinetic factor is spectral \
and whose potential factor is a pointwise phase. The double well is the \
smallest example that forces this choice, and it repays it with physics no \
moment filter can represent: the non-Gaussian conditional state, the collapse \
into one well, and the Zeno suppression of coherent tunneling set against the \
backaction heating that drives the particle over the barrier."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"487dadd0-5ed6-7873-7802-449a5b634b59"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5219761b-8a64-c9ff-0227-68452f169bc5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We started from one equation, the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger \
equation, rewrote its measurement half as a Bayesian update, and built it \
into a split-operator engine in which a single function carries the \
potential; then we ran that engine across the free particle (recovered \
exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69346765-6d1c-e9c9-18cc-7f4f04aebb13"],
 ", heating at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c22b8c2-70f4-0562-25d1-31ac00816c48"],
 "), the harmonic trap (a pure squeezed conditional state below the vacuum, \
an unconditional state that heats without bound), and the double well (a \
non-Gaussian conditional state that localizes into one well and has its \
tunneling frozen by observation while the same backaction heats it over the \
barrier). The measurement was the same in every case; only the unitary \
changed. The natural next steps are to lower the detection efficiency below \
unity, so a single record no longer purifies the conditional state and the \
trajectory becomes a mixed conditional density matrix, or to add mechanical \
damping, so the trapped unconditional state finally reaches the thermal \
steady state the bare measurement never does. Both are small edits to the \
engine you now have, and the code is yours to make them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04fec585-b88c-469b-2c85-dcef39392ce1"]
},
